Repair the complete source below and return a corrected complete `Solution.java`.

`cachedSegments(String signature)` parses a colon-separated signature and caches the result. A signature must be non-null, nonblank, and contain only nonblank segments; otherwise it throws `IllegalArgumentException`. Segment text is preserved exactly, including surrounding spaces when the segment is not blank. Results preserve segment order. The returned list must be unmodifiable so callers cannot corrupt cached results. Repeated equal signatures may return the same safe cached object.

```java
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.Arrays;
import java.util.List;
import java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;
import java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentMap;

public final class Solution {
    private static final ConcurrentMap<String, List<String>> CACHE =
            new ConcurrentHashMap<String, List<String>>();

    private Solution() {}

    public static List<String> cachedSegments(String signature) {
        if (signature == null || signature.trim().isEmpty()) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("blank signature");
        }
        List<String> existing = CACHE.get(signature);
        if (existing != null) return existing;

        List<String> parsed = new ArrayList<String>(
                Arrays.asList(signature.split(":", -1)));
        for (String segment : parsed) {
            if (segment.trim().isEmpty()) {
                throw new IllegalArgumentException("blank segment");
            }
        }
        List<String> raced = CACHE.putIfAbsent(signature, parsed);
        return raced == null ? parsed : raced;
    }
}
```

